From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:03:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Exec the loader's real path on macOS.

Wine starts every Windows process by executing <ntdll.so's directory>/wine.
In an app bundle that is a symbolic link to the bundle's executable,
Contents/MacOS/wine, and a process started through the link doesn't
belong to the bundle: Launch Services gives it no bundle identifier and
never reads the bundle's Info.plist, so macOS can't recognise a game
(LSApplicationCategoryType, Game Mode), and CFBundleGetMainBundle()
doesn't find the bundle's resources, such as the Vulkan loader's driver
manifests in Contents/Resources/vulkan/icd.d.

Resolve the path once, when the paths are set up, and execute the
bundle's executable itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
index e476231..721f23c 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -433,7 +433,14 @@ static void init_paths(void)
         if (!(dll_dir = remove_tail( ntdll_dir, get_so_dir(current_machine) ))) dll_dir = ntdll_dir;
         bin_dir = build_relative_path( dll_dir, LIBDIR "/wine", BINDIR );
         data_dir = build_relative_path( dll_dir, LIBDIR "/wine", DATADIR "/wine" );
-        wineloader = build_path( ntdll_dir, "wine" );
+        char *loader = build_path( ntdll_dir, "wine" );
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+        /* In an app bundle this is a symlink to Contents/MacOS/wine: exec the bundle's own executable, so that
+         * Launch Services sees every Wine process as the bundle's (its Info.plist, e.g. the game category). */
+        char *real = realpath( loader, NULL );
+        if (real) { free( loader ); loader = real; }
+#endif
+        wineloader = loader;
     }
 #if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__aarch64__)
     loader_is_entitled( wineloader );  /* before any fork */
